From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:27:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix #4, #22, #23: server keeps the newest read and
 survives unread bodies

- _store checks "older than the current version" before "same payload",
  and a repeat read of the same version moves ca_current.changed_at and
  ca_items.read_at/read_by forward (no ca_changes row). Before, x@08:00
  Open -> y@18:00 identical -> z@12:00 Stale stored z's stale read.
- Item changes must carry a parseable changedAt (skipped with a reason
  instead of stamped "now"); seq must be a real whole number
  (0 < seq < 2^63, bool rejected); a non-numeric Content-Length is 400.
- _reply closes the connection (Connection: close) when it answers
  before the request body was read (401/403/400), so a keep-alive
  client's next request isn't parsed out of the leftover body (#22).
- Handler.timeout = 30 so a stalled client frees its thread (#23).
- PROTOCOL.md updated; CI runs the Python tests.

Tests (test_server.py): stale read after an identical later read is
unchanged and read_at is 18:00; missing/invalid changedAt skipped;
bad seqs skipped; 403 POST then GET on one keep-alive socket, 401 the
same, and Content-Length "lots" -> 400.

